WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
mathematical research can feel very
self-indulgent and and and teaching for

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.120
me is kind of an answer to that where I
really get to share with people with

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:16.550
other people what I what I love doing I
think one one challenge is that

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:20.580
mathematics has a difficult reputation and
I think that many people are ready to

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.939
shut off as soon as they as soon as they
hear the word mathematics I get a lot of

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:27.840
negative reactions when I say that I'm a
mathematician and I really believe that

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:34.130
that that everybody can have joyful math
experiences I really believe this and

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:38.010
and it's a challenge to implement it and
and I really believe that in a classroom

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.120
you can not just tailor the class to the
students that are getting the highest

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.780
grades that everybody can really benefit
but so that's my challenge is to is to

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.350
make is to make sure that that happens
and it can be difficult when you know

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.980
you have students that you know they
have three jobs sometimes they arrive to

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.890
class hungry
they're paying for their for their

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:00.719
parents rent and they have you know the
little time that they have available to

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:07.110
do mathematics and so those realities
are are complex and and I think it's

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.689
important to remember that that doesn't
mean that this student is not talented

00:01:09.689 --> 00:01:16.890
that or not interested you know and so a
challenge and a joy is to is to get the

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:22.799
best work and out of students and to see
their full potential and I think one

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:25.470
thing that I try doing a lot is
structuring my classroom in a way that I

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:29.100
really values everybody's voice and I
think the biggest joy is when you have

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.950
somebody who's been sitting in the back
and very quiet and kind of not really a

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:38.939
very comfortable kind of speaking in
their mathematical voice and then having

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:41.820
them find their mathematical voice and
having having them find their joy and

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.579
having them kind of be able to express
themselves and that's that's really one

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:48.470
of my favorite things is and as an
educator

